  "notes": "ディスる comes from the English \"diss\" (short for \"disrespect\"), originally from hip-hop culture. It entered Japanese through rap and internet culture.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is slang primarily used by younger generations and on the internet. In formal contexts, use ⟦{批判|ひはん}する→批判する：21993_hihansuru⟧, ⟦{悪口|わるくち}→悪口：03794_warukuchi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{言|い}う→言う：00515_iu⟧, or ⟦{馬鹿|ばか}→馬鹿：03574_baka⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ディスる: to diss someone/something\n- ディスられる: to get dissed (passive)",
